This testcase verifies that the module namespace returned by a runtime
`import()` expression is correctly mapped to the module exports even if
the imported module itself statically imports another module at compile
time.

Since statically imported modules are linked into the same program, the
exports of the innermost modules occupy the leading slots of the shared
export table. The namespace builder must honor the per-source export
offset to avoid pairing symbol names with the wrong export entries.

The dependency tree is:

root
 + import: outer
    + import: inner

-- Testcase --
mod = import('outer');

printf("m = %.J\n", mod);
-- End --

-- File inner.uc --
export const value = 5;
export function fn() { return "inner"; }
-- End --

-- File outer.uc --
import { fn } from 'inner';

const local = fn();

export function f() { return "f"; }
export function g() { return "g"; }
-- End --

-- Args --
-R -L files/
-- End --

-- Expect stdout --
m = {
	"f": "function f() { ... }",
	"g": "function g() { ... }"
}
-- End --
